feat(rpmh): per-slot TCS audit, and a submit result that is not a success claim

R4.2: kebab_tcs_submit() now reports the channel it is leaving behind: OK only
when the sink completed synchronously, SINK_FAILED when the sink left ERROR or
TIMEOUT, and PENDING while the command is still in flight.  A caller can no
longer mistake submission for a confirmed rail.

R5-A2: the probe now reads the drv-level registers at +0x00/0x04/0x08/0x0C and,
per TCS, wait/control/status/enable plus both command slots.  Measured: TCS0
holds two CLK requests (0x30000 and 0x30010, status 0x010101); TCS1 has
control 0x00010000, enable 0, no commands, and no completion IRQ (irq_en is
0x00020000); prnt_chld 0x800c8104 decodes to max_tcs = 8 for drv-2, so TCS8
does not exist and the DT 2+3+3+1 has to exclude the control TCS.

Read-only: no register is written.

--- a/bsd/dev/kebab_spmi.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/kebab_spmi.c
@@ -836,6 +836,8 @@
 #define KEBAB_RSC_TCS_TOTAL     9u      /* 2 active + 3 sleep + 3 wake + 1 control */
 #define KEBAB_RSC_CMD_WAIT      0x10u
 #define KEBAB_RSC_RESP_DATA     0x40u
+#define KEBAB_RSC_IRQ_CLEAR     0x08u
+#define KEBAB_RSC_PRNT_CHLD     0x0cu
 
 #define KEBAB_RSC_IRQ_ENABLE    0x00u
 #define KEBAB_RSC_IRQ_STATUS    0x04u
@@ -921,7 +923,7 @@
